course: dictionary
lesson: 2767
title: Discourage and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Fences discourage burglars.» Here discourage means to make something less likely to happen. A fence makes a burglar less likely to break in. Look for the clue: the thing being discouraged is the thing that becomes less likely.
explain: Discourage can also mean to make someone feel less confident or less hopeful. «A bad mark can discourage a pupil», so the pupil may feel less sure they can do well. Teachers encourage pupils to keep going, and encourage is the opposite of discourage.
explain: You can also discourage someone from doing something, as in «discourage someone from climbing the wall». This means you try to stop them by showing them it is not a good idea. To check your meaning, swap in a phrase like "make less likely" or "talk someone out of" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Discourage is a verb. Its forms are discourage, discourages, discouraged and discouraging.
fact: «Discourage» means to make someone less confident or less hopeful.
fact: «Discourage» can mean to try to stop someone by showing them it is not a good idea, as in «discourage someone from doing».
fact: «Discourage» can also mean to make something less likely to happen, as in «Netting discourages birds».
fact: The opposite of «discourage» is «encourage», which means to give someone hope and confidence.
exercise: «Fences discourage burglars.» What does discourage mean here? | Make someone feel very happy | *Make something less likely to happen | Sell something quickly | Build something tall and strong
exercise: «A bad mark can discourage a pupil.» What might the pupil feel? | More confident and proud | Very hungry | *Less confident and less hopeful | Excited to go outside
exercise: Which word is the opposite of discourage? | Delay | Forget | *Encourage | Discover
test: Which phrase tells someone not to lose hope? | Put away | *Don't be discouraged | Discourage from | Put on
test: «Netting discourages birds from the garden.» What does discourage mean here? | Makes birds sing louder | Feeds the birds every day | Counts the birds as they fly | *Makes birds less likely to come
exam: Which sentence uses discourage to mean stop someone by showing them it is not a good idea? | Her friends cheered loudly when she reached the top. | *Her friends tried to discourage her from climbing the icy roof. | Her friends bought her a brand new bike.
